      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hi, thank you. Um, well, I guess what brings me in is that I just feel like I can’t settle in my own body anymore. It's really frustrating. Especially when I’m supposed to sit quietly and handle paperwork or, you know, go over shared household plans. \n\nLike the other night, we were supposed to sit down and figure out the budget for fixing up the back deck. The wood out there is completely rotting, so I was looking into that composite decking? It's so incredibly expensive now, but I spent hours looking at it and I found this one color called 'Tiki Torch' that I actually really liked. My husband thinks it's way too orange, though, and he wanted to look at the actual numbers. But anyway, he had all the spreadsheets out at the kitchen table, and I just... I couldn't just sit there in the chair with him. I had to keep getting up, wiping down the counters, checking the front porch even though it was dark out... \n\nWait, what did you ask me? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yeah, I just can't seem to sit still for that kind of stuff.",
